  "shorterRoute": "Use native finite-source Hom base change and flat tensor injection, evaluated at pure tensors. The original rational Tate finiteness theorem supplies the sole finiteness input; no dimension or basis of the root-valued target is required. Reuse native self-adjoint submodules and polynomial induction for exactly the sum of squared good-prime shifts and its projector polynomial. A direct idempotent range argument proves the needed conditional restriction statement without developing general orthogonal decomposition theory.",
  "assumptionsToDischarge": "Injectivity, alternation, good-prime adjointness and the cyclotomic multiplier of the actual original pairing after coefficient extension. The supporting restriction result retains explicit idempotence and self-adjointness assumptions until the actual transported projector supplies them.",
  "remaining": "Arithmetic primitive projector realization on the original Tate module, its nonzero rank-two image identification, primitive determinant, residual association, automorphy and all-weight continuation remain open; 16/20, DUB-17--20 OPEN.",
